course: dictionary
lesson: 160
title: Aftershock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An aftershock is a smaller earthquake that comes after a big earthquake in the same area. The ground may keep shaking for days, weeks or even longer. The context gives you the clue: the big earthquake comes first, so the smaller shake that follows is an aftershock.
explain: «After a big earthquake come many smaller aftershocks, sometimes for months or years.» Test your meaning by swapping it in: "After a big earthquake come many smaller earthquakes" still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: The word can also be used in a wider way. An aftershock can be the upsets or effects that follow a big shocking event, not just the shaking of the ground. The clue is the word after, and the shocking event that came before it.
fact: An aftershock is a smaller earthquake that comes after a big one in the same area.
fact: «Aftershocks» can carry on for months or years after a big earthquake.
fact: Aftershocks can also mean the upsets or effects that follow a big shocking event.
fact: The word is built from after and shock: something that comes after a shock.
fact: Strong aftershocks can still cause damage, so people stay careful after an earthquake.
exercise: What is an aftershock? | *A smaller earthquake that comes after a big earthquake in the same area | A loud noise made by a door slamming | A giant storm that starts a flood | A type of rock found under the sea
exercise: «After a big earthquake come many smaller aftershocks, sometimes for months or years.» How long can aftershocks last? | *Sometimes for months or years | They never last longer than a day | Only on the first morning | Only for one minute
exercise: A strong ___ can still shake buildings after the first earthquake. Which word fits the gap? | castle | *aftershock | breakfast | rainbow
test: In a news story, a town is hit by a big earthquake, then smaller shakes continue for days. What are the smaller shakes called? | Tremors of the sea | Echoes | Rain clouds | *Aftershocks
test: Which sentence uses aftershocks to mean upsets that follow a big shocking event? | We baked a cake for the school fair. | *The aftershocks of the big storm left many families worried for weeks. | The cat slept all afternoon on the sofa. | We played a game of football at break time.
exam: Which word in «After a big earthquake come many smaller aftershocks» shows that the aftershocks come later? | many | *after | smaller | earthquake
